      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Testicular pain both acute and chronic is quite common and may result from many different diseases located both in and outside of the testis. Diffuse testicular microlithiasis is a rarely encountered problem in urology and up to now a unique sonographic appearance. We here report a case with combination of both signs and give a short review of the literature."},
